      "description": "Rajasthan is a western state of India rich with historic monuments. The oldest sites are few and these are from the Harappan civilization. Post 3rd-century BCE, the heritage sites in Rajasthan are predominantly related to Hinduism along with many sites of Jainism. Rajasthan also has a few of Buddhism. As one of the states that saw repeated Hindu–Muslim wars particularly after the 12th century, many of these are in ruins. The state also witnessed many attempts to repair and the construction of new monuments that include Indo-Islamic architectural themes. The state preserves some of the early temple forms, some of the oldest known Sanskrit inscriptions in India, and many exceptionally detailed artwork reliefs about Hindu and Jain legends. The map above shows over 200 historic sites in Rajasthan with GPS coordinates. These are predominantly Hindu and Jain sites. The GPS coordinates are based on actual field survey and periodic site visits since 2014 for detailed aerial and surface photography along with architectural plans digitization effort. Map of all coordinates on OSM Export all coordinates as KML Template:Use dmy dates Template:Use Indian English List 1 of 2: Ramchandraji Mandir 24°36′14″N 72°24′56″E ﻿ / ﻿ 24.60383°N 72.415481°E ﻿ / 24.60383; 72.415481 Sun Temple, Varman 24°36′12″N 72°28′26″E ﻿ / ﻿ 24.60323°N 72.473760°E ﻿ / 24.60323; 72.473760 Ambaji Temple, Lunol 24°36′51″N 72°35′00″E ﻿ / ﻿ 24.61410°N 72.583437°E ﻿ / 24.61410; 72.583437 Dilwara Temples, Mount Abu 24°36′34″N 72°43′23″E ﻿ / ﻿ 24.60938°N 72.722979°E ﻿ / 24.60938; 72.722979 Ranakpur Jain Temple, Ranakpur 25°06′56″N 73°28′22″E ﻿ / ﻿ 25.11565°N 73.472873°E ﻿ / 25.11565; 73.472873 Jain old Temple 25°06′58″N 73°28′18″E ﻿ / ﻿ 25.11601°N 73.471537°E ﻿ / 25.11601; 73.471537 Lohargal Sun Temple, Ranakpur 25°06′51″N 73°28′13″E ﻿ / ﻿ 25.11429°N 73.470329°E ﻿ / 25.11429; 73.470329 Surya Mandir, Mandesar 24°36′59″N 73°54′37″E ﻿ / ﻿ 24.61638°N 73.910154°E ﻿ / 24.61638; 73.910154 Kailashpur